# Field Tests
## 13/10/2024
### GNSS & IMU SHARC Buoy compared to Datawell Waverider MkII

Latitude       : -34 12.24S
Longitude      : 018 17.20E
Water Depth    : 70m

GNSS Valid Data: 13:04 - 13:50 & 14:38 - 14:57

IMU Valid Data: 14:38 - 15:03

NB! Both SHARC bouys underestimated the significant wave height compared to the Waverider. Loss in accuracy attributed to:
	- Moored vs free-drifting
	- Tether pulling the top of the buoys over when under tension (tether attached above the vertical centre of the buoy)
	- Instability of the drum in which the SHARC buoys were placed.

Nevertheless, the underestimation is cause for concern.
	